Kalandra is a fresh continuation of the Clio language project by Pouya Eghbali and contributors.
Clio: https://github.com/clio-lang/clio

The initial website scaffold and supporting card components come from Tiramisu Docs (Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/pouya-eghbali/tiramisu-docs
Scaffold source revision: c5a3ca2b59f7845a75d9de38a4cfa4cf8763315a

Native project manifest parsing uses toml++ 3.4.0 (MIT), by Mark Gillard:
https://github.com/marzer/tomlplusplus/tree/v3.4.0
The license is retained in native/third-party/tomlplusplus-LICENSE.

Experimental Vulkan runtime shaders reuse the MIT-licensed ggml/llama.cpp sources:
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/tree/a91eab67d8389d979d29fdf6633b2edd0718eb4b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders
The original license and per-file hashes are retained in native/vulkan/third_party/ggml/.
